@@ -15,3 +15,30 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## WebMCP
+
+In a browser with WebMCP enabled, the site exposes these tools after client hydration:
+
+| Tool | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `list_articles` | All article slugs, titles, summaries, images, and URLs. |
+| `get_article` | Details for a required `slug`, plus body text when that article is open. |
+| `get_reading_list` | Article details for the current session's saved articles. |
+| `toggle_reading_list` | Adds or removes a required article `slug`, returning the updated list. |
+| `open_search` | Opens the search flyout and exposes its `search_articles` form tool. |
+| `open_reading_list` | Opens the reading list and exposes removal form tools for saved articles. |
+
+The search form accepts a required `query` and returns matching titles/summaries and
+article URLs. Bookmark forms (`toggle_bookmark_<slug>`) and reading-list removal
+forms (`remove_bookmark_<slug>`) operate on their displayed article and return the
+updated list of slugs. These forms use `toolautosubmit` and pass results back through
+`SubmitEvent.respondWith()` for agent submissions. Human submissions use the same
+handlers, and all bookmark controls stay synchronized with tool updates.
+
+JavaScript tools feature-detect `document.modelContext` (with a fallback for older
+`navigator.modelContext` implementations). They unregister on component unmount
+or Astro page transitions. Unsupported browsers retain the normal UI.
+
+API references: [declarative forms](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api)
+and [JavaScript tools](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api).
